1
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:09,100
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:31,540
You're on the move!

3
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,960
Looks like the end of the line for you!

4
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,500
What's so funny?

5
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,697
Take a look at your Celtic Guardian!

6
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,560
He's just not himself anymore!

7
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:22,840
He transformed my only
monster into a cocoon!

8
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:26,119
He must be planning to hatch
another insect monster!

9
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,840
I play polymerization!

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Allowing me to fuse my knight and my
dragon to form Gaia, the Dragon Champion!

11
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,420
Now, Gaia, attack!

12
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,180
Hold on!

13
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,240
You just triggered my trap!

14
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,140
DNA Surgery!

15
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,420
What's that?

16
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:54,000
Just what I needed to win this duel.

17
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,817
It lets me change every monster
on the field into an insect,

18
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,400
Including your dragon champion!

19
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:08,880
And as you know, my insect
barrier blocks all insect attacks!

20
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:13,814
Weevil has me trapped!

21
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,512
Now every monster I summon becomes a bug!

22
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:21,484
So as long as this insect barrier is in
play, none of my attacks will get through!

23
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:26,217
You beat this guy once
and you can do it again!

24
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,680
He's stronger now.

25
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:29,100
Come on.

26
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:38,520
Dude, you got three Toons
breathing down your neck.

27
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:41,697
You better think of something
before you're extinct.

28
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:42,720
Gee, thanks.

29
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:45,980
You're in way over your head.

30
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:49,600
Thanks to the seal of
Aurichalcos, I can never be beat.

31
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:50,900
But enough talk.

32
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,140
On with the duel.

33
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,440
It's showtime. First,

34
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,037
I'll use Polymerization to combine my

35
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:01,120
Gilosaurus with my Kytoptera
to form Pornsaurus.

36
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:06,240
But you ain't seen nothing yet.

37
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,480
Next, I'll play Giant Rex.

38
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:14,760
And a Seal of Orichalcos gives
my Jurassic Giants a power boost.

39
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,437
Time to get prehistoric on you, Wheeler.

40
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:22,837
By letting my ravenous
meat-eaters chow down on

41
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:27,660
your life points My
Horn-Saurus is up first Now,

42
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,480
attack Wheeler directly

43
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:34,560
How can he do that when you've
got a monster on the field?

44
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,230
Easy,

45
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:39,517
Horn-Saurus has a special
ability That lets him bypass

46
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:43,720
your monsters and go straight
for your life points Tough break

47
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:53,260
That runt is kicking your butt.

48
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,537
Thanks for the help.

49
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:55,679
You're a real pal.

50
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,998
For my next trick, Giant Rex will
make your panther warrior disappear.

51
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,040
That was your last monster.

52
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,479
Your cheerleading skills need work.

53
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,800
Mind if I interrupt you two?

54
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:14,640
It's still my turn.

55
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,840
And it's only fair to let my
gilosaurus have his shot now.

56
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,300
I activate Skategold!

57
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,120
I've always hated those hairballs.

58
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:35,620
And they've always hated you, too.

59
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,488
I thought you were a goner.

60
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:40,580
Next time, warn me when
you're gonna save yourself.

61
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,000
Weevil, look out!

62
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,973
Thanks for the warning.

63
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,240
Now, back to the game!

64
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:57,620
I activate the magic card cell
division, and I'll use it on my Legul!

65
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:00,580
Oh, no!

66
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:06,880
Thanks to my cell division card, I
have two leeches for the price of one!

67
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,197
If you actually thought I'd be frightened

68
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,920
by a monster with a
mere 800 attack points,

69
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,454
you're sadly mistaken!

70
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:19,780
I'm disappointed.

71
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:23,667
I thought you, of all people,
would recognize a good strategy.

72
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:26,999
But I guess what I heard
about you is true, Pharaoh.

73
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:32,107
Without Yugi's help, you're
nothing but a second-rate wannabe.

74
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:41,966
As soon as I win this duel, you'll be
locked away forever with your better half.

75
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:45,957
Please, you don't stand a
chance, you little cockroach.

76
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,275
Why, thank you, Taya!

77
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:50,297
The roach is one of the
strongest insects alive!

78
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,400
All right, then prove it!

79
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:55,517
Yeah, if you're so tough,
then show us what you've got!

80
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,000
And stop talking about it! Very well!

81
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:04,100
I sacrificed my pheromone wasp and my
leghole in order to summon my insect queen!

82
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,220
Long live the queen!

83
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:17,360
And now for her crown,
the mark of the Oritaltos

84
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:23,337
And let's not forget about her
highness's special ability She receives

85
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,840
a whopping 200 extra attack points
for every insect monster on the field

86
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:34,637
So that's 400 for my two insects
Plus another 400 for the two

87
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:40,380
insects on your side of the field
For a grand total of 3,500 points

88
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:45,680
Now it's the strongest creature in
play Yes, but before it attacks,

89
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:46,998
I've got a surprise

90
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,460
Legul, suck him

91
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:51,810
Surprise!

92
00:06:51,893 --> 00:06:54,680
It jumps over your defense
and strikes you directly

93
00:06:57,260 --> 00:07:02,820
Now that it's served its purpose, I'll
sacrifice my Legul so my queen can attack

94
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:08,540
Now, Insect Queen, attack
his dragon champion

95
00:07:16,860 --> 00:07:20,448
Since your monster's gone, my
queen loses some attack points.

96
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:23,200
But I gained something even more precious.

97
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,430
Gross.

98
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:31,680
My prehistoric pets are
gonna walk all over you.

99
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,400
Save it, Geekasaurus.

100
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:37,237
I've got more talent in my left
nostril than you'll ever have.

101
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,160
Look, Wheeler.

102
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,940
The Seal of Aurichalcos is on my side,

103
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:43,981
so I've got more power
than you and your nostrils.

104
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,680
Anyway, my move.

105
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:49,980
I summon Rocket Warrior in defense mode.

106
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,818
Then I'll place two cards face down.

107
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:57,077
Now clear something up for me, would you?

108
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,600
Yeah, what do you want?

109
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:01,537
Is this duel really worth
that much to you, Rex?

110
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:05,357
I mean, you're risking your own
soul just for a chance to defeat me.

111
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:06,457
I know what I'm doing.

112
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:09,540
I'm earning the respect
I deserve, Wheeler.

113
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:13,337
Because ever since you knocked me out
of the Duelist Kingdom tournament,

114
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:16,260
I've been mocked,
ridiculed, and humiliated.

115
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,480
But that's all gonna end here.

116
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:21,300
I am sick and tired of being a loser.

117
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,120
Wait a sec.

118
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,438
That speech sounds kind of familiar.

119
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:28,060
I told you the Mai you knew is gone.

120
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,860
I traded in her soul for power.

121
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:33,937
The old Mai was too lonely and pathetic.

122
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:36,440
The girl was just holding me back.

123
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:41,240
This darts guy must prey on people's
weaknesses by promising them power.

124
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:43,400
Rex, hold on.

125
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:45,200
Save it, punk.

126
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,220
You'll never stop this duel.

127
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:50,360
Now, Horn-Saurus, attack.

128
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:53,940
You just triggered my trap.

129
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,380
Activate magic arm shield.

130
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,480
Yes again, Wheeler.

131
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,840
I've got a trap, too.

132
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:06,240
Go, Jurassic Heart!

133
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,640
What was that?

134
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:16,100
It cancels out any trap
used against a dinosaur.

135
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,580
So your monster's history.

136
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,580
But wait, that's not all.

137
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:25,140
Giant Rex, attack!

138
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:27,900
Trample his puny scapegoat.

139
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:33,020
Now, Gilosaurus, it's time
to see what you can do.

140
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:42,420
Next, I'll place one card
face down and end my turn.

141
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:47,080
Now you're one attack away
from losing your soul forever!

142
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,160
My move, Rex.

143
00:09:55,820 --> 00:10:00,408
It's my Red-Eyes Black Dragon, the card
I won from Rex back in Dula's kingdom.

144
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,521
This could be just what I needed.

145
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:06,460
I sacrifice my last scapegoat.

146
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,320
Then I activate Star Blaster.

147
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:14,518
Now all I have to do is add
one to the number I roll,

148
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:17,444
and I can summon a monster
with that many stars.

149
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:26,850
Yes!

150
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:28,194
Read it and wait, pal.

151
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,960
Last I checked, six plus one was seven.

152
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,500
So here comes a seven-star monster.

153
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:37,138
It's gonna take more than
dumb luck to win this duel.

154
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,928
You got a point there, Rex.

155
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,709
Well, maybe this can help.

156
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,000
Look familiar, Dino Brain?

157
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,520
It's my Red-Eyes Black Dragon.

158
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:52,260
Yep, he's back. Better than ever.

159
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:56,533
Because I'm enhancing his
power with my Metal Morph card.

160
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:59,240
Now old Red-Eyes gets a 300-point boost.

161
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:03,342
Plus, whenever he attacks a monster,
he absorbs half its strength.

162
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:09,880
Now for the fun part.

163
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,046
Let me simplify this for you.

164
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:15,637
When my dragon blows your old
fossil back to the Stone Age,

165
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,980
his power grows by half of 2,500.

166
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:20,540
Take it away, red eyes.

167
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,980
I'm back into extinction for you.

168
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:30,200
Nice one, man.

169
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,520
Next, I'll place one card face down

170
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,900
And that's all for now

171
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:45,977
My insect army is slowly
infesting the playing field

172
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:51,140
Just a few more turns and
you're bug bait We'll see Yeah,

173
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,720
people like you never win What's this?

174
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,017
More comments from the peanut gallery?

175
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:58,837
Tell me, what is a person like me?

176
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:01,460
You're a greedy, power-hungry worm.

177
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,935
What's that make you?

178
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:07,057
Correct me if I'm wrong, but aren't
you the one who wanted power?

179
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:11,240
So much that you sold out your
best friend just for a taste of it?

180
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,760
Watch it, bug boy.

181
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:17,617
I'm just telling you what I witnessed
firsthand during your last duel, that's all.

182
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:20,818
You were determined to win
at all costs, weren't you?

183
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:23,840
So you activated the seal of Oricalcos,

184
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:28,472
even though you knew you were endangering
the life of someone close to you.

185
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,180
Now that's what I call
power hungry and greedy.

186
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:36,420
Well, this time the seal and
all of its powers belong to me.

187
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,300
You're not scaring anyone.

188
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:43,697
If you think you can win this duel
by playing your little head games,

189
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,297
then you're sorely mistaken,

190
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:46,210
Weevil.

191
00:12:46,293 --> 00:12:47,260
I'm too smart for that.

192
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:51,237
What you refer to as head games, I
call opening you up to the truth.

193
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:55,438
And whether you realize it or not,
it's causing you to doubt yourself.

194
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,897
Not that I blame you.

195
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,977
I'd be shaking in fear also.

196
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:05,280
If I were the one about
to lose his soul, that is.

197
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:15,197
Now that Red Eyes is here,
you're an endangered species.

198
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,162
It was nice knowing you, Raptor.

199
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,537
You've got some nerve
using that against me.

200
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:24,149
That dragon was my best card
until you took it away from me.

201
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,040
Hey, relax.

202
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,382
I won that card fair and square.

203
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:31,100
Go, Time Wizard!

204
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,775
Fossilize his dragon!

205
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:38,800
Red Eyes, you feeling all right?

206
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,560
You've ruined my life.

207
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,660
I used to be a regional
duel monsters champion.

208
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:54,729
At one time, Weevil and I were the most
famous duelists in the whole country.

209
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:57,940
We couldn't walk one block
without being recognized.

210
00:13:58,800 --> 00:13:59,737
I'm a holographic.

211
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:01,357
Hey, does anyone have a pen?

212
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,560
I can't wait to go.

213
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:07,280
I can't believe they're walking
down the street like regular guys.

214
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,504
Yeah, you think they'd
have a limo or something?

215
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,820
Soon, everyone in the world will envy me.

216
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:20,380
I'll be back on top, just like I was
before you defeated me in Duelist Kingdom.

217
00:14:20,740 --> 00:14:23,797
I'll be Weevil Underwood,
the new king of games.

218
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,040
It has a nice ring, doesn't it?

219
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:30,566
I almost forgot what it feels
like to be worshipped and adored.

220
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,540
Weevil, Rex?

221
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,940
Can I have your autographs?

222
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,840
I'm a huge fan of your work.

223
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,040
You talking to us?

224
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,620
Well, of course he is.

225
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:43,400
Now you do the honors, Rex. Sure.

226
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,140
Thanks a lot. You guys rock.

227
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:50,700
We're not giving these
things away for free, kid.

228
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,700
It'll cost you your rarest card.

229
00:14:53,880 --> 00:14:54,720
What?

230
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,060
My card?

231
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,880
Uh, thanks, I think.

232
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:06,960
Unfortunately, my fame didn't last.

233
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,860
I became a joke.

234
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:10,512
How could I lose to you?

235
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,320
What do you mean by that?

236
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:16,777
I was supposed to win the most prestigious
dueling tournament ever thrown,

237
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:18,997
and instead I was defeated by a rookie.

238
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,817
I went in as a champion,

239
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:25,200
but I came out as the laughingstock
of the entire dueling world.

240
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:28,422
I was knocked out of the
tournament in round one.

241
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:30,880
Hey, check it out.

242
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:32,568
It's Bug Boy and Dino Dork.

243
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:37,699
Can you believe those two are actually
showing their faces in public?

244
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:40,960
Some fans.

245
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,612
The second we lost, they all disappeared.

246
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:46,520
This stinks!

247
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:49,900
We lost everything to
a couple of newcomers.

248
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,640
No more movie premieres.

249
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,220
No more private parties.

250
00:15:56,740 --> 00:16:00,540
Hey, you Rex and Weevil? Who's asking? Me!

251
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:05,738
Is this the card they took from you?

252
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,040
Yep, that's the one. Thanks again.

253
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:11,617
What'd you do with
those autographs anyway?

254
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:14,406
Please, I couldn't even
get those things away.

255
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:19,180
That was the lowest point of my life.

256
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,140
Since then, it's been one
bad day after another.

257
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:28,180
I was a household name,
and now I'm nothing.

258
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:31,940
And I owe it all to you, Joey Wheeler!

259
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,020
Are you finished yet?

260
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,560
I'm sick of hearing your sob story.

261
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,160
I'm supposed to feel bad for you?

262
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:43,337
Just because you think that it's my
fault you're not popular anymore?

263
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:44,837
Get a life, will ya?

264
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,360
That's the point! What's the point?

265
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:49,208
That you don't have a life?

266
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:50,690
Exactly!

267
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:54,060
You took my life away from
me, and now I want it back!

268
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:56,987
You've got no one to
blame but yourself, Rex.

269
00:16:57,460 --> 00:17:00,397
Don't you see you're dueling
for the wrong reasons?

270
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:03,880
To me, this game is about
striving to be my best.

271
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:06,960
It's taught me to trust myself.

272
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,660
And to keep trying, no
matter how tough things get.

273
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:14,017
And let me tell you, things have
gotten pretty tough out there.

274
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:16,420
I never gave up, no matter what.

275
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,470
What?

276
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:23,637
Can't handle the fact that Duel Monsters
isn't all about fame and fortune?

277
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,249
Annoyed because you
had the game all wrong?

278
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:29,580
Wow, you're even lamer than I remember.

279
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:35,880
I mean, you give the term goody-two-shoes
an entirely new meaning, Wheeler.

280
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:39,200
I realized a long time ago that being Mr.

281
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,889
Nice Guy gets you nowhere.

282
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:45,334
That's why I decided to team
up with Darts and his gang.

283
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:49,900
They gave me something I could
never get just by playing fair.

284
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:55,520
The power I need to finally win back
everything that you took away from me, Wheeler!

285
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,958
I guess you'll never learn, will ya?

286
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,820
Let's just move on, shall we?

287
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,397
It's party time! Look out!

288
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:10,400
I sacrifice Gilosaurus and Giant
Rex, so I can summon Tyrant Dragon!

289
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:20,080
And thanks to the Seal of Aurichalcos,
it gets an extra 500 attack points!

290
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,820
Look at that!

291
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:25,380
We both have Giant Dragons now!

292
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:28,760
But only one's gonna remain standing!

293
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,720
What's wrong, Pharaoh?

294
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,805
Feel like your life is
spinning out of control?

295
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,020
Well, maybe that's because it is.

296
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,220
But it'll all be over soon.

297
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:49,740
Enough! My move!

298
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,664
But first, a friendly reminder.

299
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:55,258
Two turns have passed since
my cocoon first appeared.

300
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:58,360
It won't be long now before it hatches.

301
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:02,716
And when it does, you'll meet the
same fate as your little buddy, Yugi.

302
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,598
I've never meant for this to happen.

303
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,740
Now I summon Karibu!

304
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:15,500
That means my insect queen
gains 200 more points!

305
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:20,820
Remember, my DNA trap card
turns all your monsters to bugs!

306
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:24,680
I place one card face down!

307
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:32,900
Be patient, Great Leviathan.

308
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:36,360
Soon the soul of the
pharaoh shall be yours.

309
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:45,180
You're about to pay the ultimate price,

310
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:49,560
and I'll be known as the duelist
who dethroned the king of games!
